From 58c9a75fd8ab2b72059d39936be7d171cd1d8a4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael.B" <xiaoxufeng@espressif.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:46:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sdio_slave): stop the recv link before resetting it on
 start

sdio_slave_hal_load_buf() issues txlink_restart for every buffer after
the first one. When sdio_slave_start() runs while such a restart is still
pending, slc0_tx_rst does not clear it and the txlink_start written right
after the reset can be lost: the link stays parked and never fetches a
descriptor, so the host's writes are never received.

Stop the recv link in sdio_slave_hal_recv_start() before the reset to
drop the pending restart.

Add standalone cases to the sdio slave test app, which need no host:
- recv: load buffers before sdio_slave_start() and check that the recv
  link leaves park. With the new opt_perf config (-O2), this fails on
  ESP32-C5 without the fix.
- send: queue packets before or after sdio_slave_start() and check that
  the send link is on one of the queued buffers. The send link is never
  restarted, so it does not have this issue; the case covers its start
  sequence.
---
 .../sdio/sdio_common_tests/README.md          |   2 +-
 .../sdio/sdio_common_tests/pytest_sdio.py     |  13 +-
 .../sdio/main/test_sdio_slave.c               | 117 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../sdio/sdkconfig.ci.opt_perf                |   2 +
 components/esp_hal_sd/sdio_slave_hal.c        |   3 +
 5 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 components/esp_driver_sdio/test_apps/sdio/sdio_common_tests/sdio/sdkconfig.ci.opt_perf

